# How to cite Mapsurvey. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository" (APA, BibTeX);
# Zenodo reads it when a release is archived. Keep it in step with
# help/src/content/docs/reference/citing-mapsurvey.md (survey/tests/test_help_site.py checks both).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mapsurvey in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Mapsurvey
abstract: >-
  Mapsurvey is an open-source platform for participatory mapping surveys:
  respondents answer by marking places, drawing routes and outlining areas
  on a map, and every answer lands on one map with its survey answers.
authors:
  - family-names: Koniukhov
    given-names: Artem
    email: konuchovartem@mapsurvey.org
url: "https://mapsurvey.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ganjasan/mapsurvey"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - participatory mapping
  - PPGIS
  - public participation GIS
  - map survey
  - citizen engagement
  - GeoDjango
